# unsafe-typecast-without-is is OFF by default (heuristic); the sibling
# unsafe-typecast-without-is.config.json enables it via "enabled": [...] so this
# fixture exercises it. FIRES on an unguarded hard cast of an object reference to
# a DIFFERENT class:
#   line 12  TButton(Sender)  -- Sender:TObject downcast, no 'Sender is TButton'
#   line 15  TButton(E)       -- E:TEdit cross-cast, no 'E is TButton'
# Must NOT fire when guarded (14, 'Sender is TComboBox' on line 13), on a TObject
# upcast (16), on the redundant same-type cast (17, TEdit(E) where E:TEdit), or a
# value/alias cast whose target is not a class (18, TColor).
unsafe-typecast-without-is 12
unsafe-typecast-without-is 15
!unsafe-typecast-without-is 14
!unsafe-typecast-without-is 16
!unsafe-typecast-without-is 17
!unsafe-typecast-without-is 18
